  "scope": "Task `89ab40aedfe4`, production source VERSION `2.0.0`, SHA-256 `2800dab77009ba054309c218507cd1e4a735860dc0f790ade8399d33888deb6b`.\nResult: built a separate opt-in legend-selected sorting prototype; production generator and canonical authority are unchanged.\nPublic parent: `d59b0160`; transferred dependency is \u201ca legend selects participants,\u201d not its erase operation.\nDefault `all_slots` is byte-for-byte canonical; proposed `contains_key` fixes the key/nonmatches and stable-sorts matching later columns.\nLesson shape: three demonstrations plus four distinct queries per setting, with the hidden setting fixed once per episode.\nExact verifier: 28/28 Racket executions matched the Python mirrors; all 14 inputs distinguished the two settings.\nAdversarial pass: 70/70 additional Racket executions across five seeds and 10/10 export-separation cases passed.\nFocused selected-task suite: 81 tests passed; no remaining test failures.\nSupplementary ticket `ticket-38db77cf6dbb4cae`: retained bbox-shortcut audit claim reproduced; existing audit remains unresolved.\nSupplementary ticket `ticket-70f1dc15c86799d9`: current-source lawful witness refutes global eligible-color frequency (`9`) versus plus census (`2`).\nNeeds attention: this is prototype-only evidence over a fixed six-slot grammar, not production approval or universal identifiability.\n",
